{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-rb:000039:note_appended:bob-cli-rb.4:0a0fd74ea3c5683b93147871988624a227ebf72d683b34f9b9c519160395601d","timestamp":"2026-11-28T01:33:08Z","actor":"bob-cli-rb.4--4","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-rb.4","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Verified two-step native lead accept: applying a lead-bearing accept inserts the type-lead marker and the lead as two native undo groups bound to the response snapshot. TypeLeadPeel Backspace peels the lead in one key. Control-Return and Command-Return skip the lead. Hosted tests cover accept, peel, skip-lead, and the undo-group split. closeUndoGroupAfter runs on the marker edit only, so marker, lead, and peel are separate ⌘Z steps without leaving an empty group that eats undo.\n\nGates: just portable-check 2925 passed / 1 skipped / 0 failures; just docs-check under the 6000-word cap; Mac scratch bundle.sh plus just typecheck-tests on the Swift sources.\n\nMeeting-notes flake: testOutOfOrderPreviewCannotReplaceNewEventSelection now asserts an order-independent Set of event tokens {old#^event, new#^event}; the generation guard still holds.\n\nmacos-ci-check green on snapshot SHA 15c7423d628b65702e61c81f1a5fa06f6ae63c06 (identical tree to bob-mac-capture HEAD 6c545f23). Workflow https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-mac-capture/actions/runs/46091145714: Lint, Build, Test, Bundle, Verify plist and signature, Launch smoke test, Install and reinstall all passed. Parent epic bob-cli-rb stays open."}}
